set heading(numbering: none)

`cross` · strike · a fixed variant.

# Form

`x.cross` on a symbol, `(a + b).cross` on a group. A recipe has one base and up to three operations.

# Examples

| Recipe | Result | Glyph |
|:--|:-:|:--|
| `h.cross` | $h.cross$ | font glyph U+210F |
| `in.cross` | $in.cross$ | built and cached |

# Four layers

| Layer | For this operation |
|:--|:--|
| Meaning | A fixed variant. A guideline, not a rule. |
| Style | Use a `sym` to give a recipe a short name. |
| Construction | A line through the base. |
| Glyph | The font glyph when the font has one, otherwise a built glyph kept in the recipe cache. |

# Rules

- More than three operations on one base gives a warning.

# From LaTeX

`\hbar` becomes `h.cross`.

